 {"id":"fabro-8c1e","title":"Revisor + closeout prompts: document sd priority number->band mapping (1=High, 2=Medium, default 2)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:20:09.207Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:20:09.207Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"sd's --priority is a 0-4 number (P0-P4) where 1=High, 2=Medium, 3=Low, default 2 - NOT intuitive at filing time. Run 01M20RX5E6P91DRT64CRCMAHGQ file v1 painpoint: 'sd create output reports Medium priority though both findings requested priority 2 - verify sd's priority number->band mapping in the CLI help before filing if exact High/Medium matters' (fabro-e4c4 and fabro-a08a landed Medium though the revisor's intent read as High-band work). IN-SESSION REPRODUCTION (agent sweep, 2026-09-08 evening): the agent filed fabro-8d1c with --priority 2 intending High and had to correct it to 1 afterwards - same trap, second consumer.\n\nFIX: one documentation line in .fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts/file.md tracker command reference (sd create row): 'priority bands: 0=P0 1=High 2=Medium 3=Low 4=Lowest; default 2 - pass 1 explicitly for High findings'. Optionally the same line in the develop closeout prompt where seeds get filed. Docs-only.\n\nBasis: journal .fabro/journal/01M20RX5E6P91DRT64CRCMAHGQ.jsonl file v1 painpoint + agent reproduction (fabro-8d1c priority correction), agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-88a4","title":"Revisor: give the Ask-Fabro analyst an open-backlog digest so it stops re-deriving known findings","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:20:09.351Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:20:09.351Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Run 01M20QA6PBYAGR1TG8MGR8KGTF analyze v1 painpoint: 6 of 7 actionable Ask-Fabro analyst recommendations duplicated already-open seeds (fabro-06e0, fabro-meta-c9f2, fabro-c3b4, fabro-4811, fabro-8275, fabro-cf03); the tracker check caught them all, but the analyst re-derived known findings because Ask-Fabro has NO backlog awareness - every pass pays the analyst tokens to rediscover the backlog, and the duplicate-guard load shifts to the file node. Run 01M20XGWE2ZYM9ADRM2PVE322F saw the same shape (7 of 8 recs dropped as duplicates).\n\nFIX: feed the target run's Ask-Fabro analyst a compact digest of open revision-labelled seeds (id + title, one line each - the same view sd list --format compact gives, but scoped to the revision label with an explicit raised limit) so it reviews the run AGAINST the backlog instead of re-discovering it. Surface lives where the revisor analyze node composes the fabro_ask prompt (.fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts - check analyze.md); keep the digest in the prompt body, not a new tool.\n\nBasis: journals .fabro/journal/01M20QA6PBYAGR1TG8MGR8KGTF.jsonl and 01M20XGWE2ZYM9ADRM2PVE322F.jsonl analyze v1, agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-dd29","title":"fabro-server tests: convention/lint that execute_run tests pin run.environment id=local (no Docker-socket deps in gate sandboxes)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:20:09.452Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:54:09.951Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Run 01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP implementer v2 painpoint: fabro-server tests that execute runs in-process with default settings depend on a Docker daemon and hard-fail in Docker-less gate sandboxes (lib/apps/fabro-server/src/server/tests.rs:8963/9086 failed with WorkflowError 'Socket not found: /var/run/docker.sock'); the run applied a 6-line [run.environment] id = \"local\" pin as adjacent repair (documented, legitimate), but nothing stops NEW execute_run tests from silently reintroducing the Docker dependency - the same class will keep bouncing gates. Distinct from fabro-fc1b (prompt rule: WHICH test suite runs) - this seed is about test AUTHORING convention so the dependency never enters.\n\nFIX: (a) convention note in the testing strategy or crate-level test docs: tests that reach execute_run/Handler::dispatch with a real provider must pin [run.environment] id = \"local\" (precedent: cancel_during_startup_persists_cancelled_reason); (b) optional cheap lint: a tests.rs grep gate in qualitygate.nu flagging execute_run test fns lacking the local-environment pin. Also record the adjacent trap already journaled: mode = \"dry_run\" coerces the provider to Local BUT routes Handler::dispatch to simulate(), so handlers' execute() never runs - assertions on observation vectors silently pass (mulch engine.jsonl already carries this).\n\nBasis: journal .fabro/journal/01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP.jsonl implementer v2 painpoint, agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.\n\nPROVENANCE (user question 2026-09-08 evening): both failing tests are OURS, fork-only (not in upstream/main), introduced BY the ADR-0019.6 security hardening line on 2026-09-08 morning: run_start_grants_github_token_bridge_only_to_user_principals landed in 919b0d18c (fabro-e505 wire test, 08:52) and worker_principal_run_without_vault_token_takes_no_token_path in 9d1ae6162 (fabro-c274, 09:09, direct agent work). The failure picture is therefore NEW since the hardening - but it is a test-infrastructure dependency, not a regression of the gate logic: these are the first in-process execute_run wire tests of this shape, they execute REAL runs, and without an explicit environment pin those runs default to the Docker provider. Local dev machines have Docker (tests green via Docker, which is why the error was never seen locally); the failure only manifests in Docker-less contexts. First exposure: run 01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP tester@1 (15:31), the first lib/-touching develop run after the tests landed - earlier passes that morning were prompts-only (fmt-only degraded gate).","labels":["engine"]}
+{"id":"fabro-3c6c","title":"Cost-tier implementer smoke checks: parse-level proof for config-only seeds, sized timeouts for built checks","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:35.888Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:35.888Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md` step 4, add: config-only seeds (no Rust touched) satisfy the smoke check with a parse-level verification (tomllib or toml parse) — never build binaries to validate config; if a built check is genuinely required, never `cargo run` cold — `cargo build` once with `timeout_ms >= 600000` then invoke `target/debug/<bin>`, and a timed-out build is not a failure (retry once with a doubled timeout; only a non-zero exit is). Mirror one cheapest-first line in `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` step 6 so briefs stop listing the expensive option first. Evidence: implementer verified a 12-line TOML edit with a 173ms tomllib parse (seq 98), then still ran `cargo run ... validate` which timed out at 180.3s with zero output and re-ran as a 416.9s build (seq 99-115); tool time 600s of the 741s run (81%), total 12m21s and $0.146. Expected effect: this class of run finishes in ~4 min instead of ~12, saving 8-10 min wall and one wasted diagnosis LLM turn per config-only seed. Distinct from open fabro-a67f (whitelist + conditional spec re-fetch) and closed fabro-513e (repo-side just recipe). Basis: run 01M2183254XQ3HJ45SR4P1Y2X6, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit 0dc16012c16ee2f6b2e61ecc73afcf0bd5f26b3d","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-c419","title":"Wire the planner's fabro_runs_list binding — the in-flight-PR guard silently fails open","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:43.290Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:43.290Z","description":"Node `planner` in `.fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro` declares `fabro_tools=\"fabro_runs_list\"` but the tool never reaches the agent: make the engine honor the node-level `fabro_tools` attribute (or set run-level `agent.fabro_tools` for develop), and until then reword planner.md step 4 to instruct journaling the degraded mode and proceeding when the tool is absent from the toolset, instead of implying the call is always possible. Evidence: this run's events seq 27 show `agent.tools.available` for planner@1 lists no fabro_runs_list and run settings show `agent.fabro_tools=false`; the planner's only journaled painpoint was that the in-flight-PR check degraded to a no-op — the exact failure closed fabro-06e0 and fabro-d0c7 were meant to prevent (fabro-22e4 double-pick while a PR waits in gate). Expected effect: the loop's only double-work guard actually functions, preventing a duplicated run (~$0.15 plus ~12 min each) next time a seed's PR sits in gate. ADR-0019: this finding changes a tool allowlist in an agent-reachable surface, so it is capability-affecting — implementation awaits explicit user approval. Fix direction is engine-mediated and read-only (the engine exposes its existing `fabro_runs_list` read tool via the node-level attribute); no raw clients or tokens proposed. Note: the run-level-warning sub-item duplicates open fabro-5b0a and is deliberately excluded. Basis: run 01M2183254XQ3HJ45SR4P1Y2X6, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit 0dc16012c16ee2f6b2e61ecc73afcf0bd5f26b3d","labels":["needs-user","revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-fe15","title":"Bake a debug fabro-cli (or shared cargo cache) into the run toolchain image","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:50.145Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:50.145Z","description":"In the `fabro-toolchain:noble` Dockerfile used for develop run containers (`.fabro/Dockerfile*`), pre-build `fabro-cli` in debug profile or mount a shared cargo cache across run containers so `target/debug/fabro` exists at container start. Evidence: this run's implementer probed `ls target/debug/fabro` and found nothing (seq 107) — the container starts with an empty `target/`, so any run legitimately needing the CLI pays ~7 min of cold build; the workflow graph comment already measures a cold gate at ~15 min worst case. Expected effect: the first cargo invocation in every run drops from minutes to seconds, independent of prompt compliance; complements the config-only smoke cost-tiering for seeds that still need built checks. Distinct from open fabro-cfd6 (prebuilt cargo-chef image for the CI gate, not run containers) and closed fabro-513e (human-facing just recipe). ADR-0019: this finding adds a binary to the agent-reachable toolchain image surface, so it is capability-affecting — implementation awaits explicit user approval. Fix direction stays engine-mediated (image build content / engine-managed cache mount; the prebuilt binary is the repo's own read-write CLI, no new credentials or external clients). Basis: run 01M2183254XQ3HJ45SR4P1Y2X6, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit 0dc16012c16ee2f6b2e61ecc73afcf0bd5f26b3d","labels":["needs-user","revision"]}
